From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] api-impl: SensorManager on Linux IIO

The SensorManager stub returned a fake Sensor for any type and only wired
up the accelerometer: a GLib timeout on the main thread read sysfs (reads
can block, e.g. while a sensor hub powers a sensor up) and listeners could
never be unregistered.

New backend (android/hardware/IioSensors.java): every device below
/sys/bus/iio/devices ($ATL_IIO_ROOT overrides it, e.g. for tests with a
fake tree) is checked for accelerometer (in_accel_{x,y,z}_raw), gyroscope
(in_anglvel_*), magnetometer (in_magn_*), light (in_illuminance[0]_raw or
_input) and proximity (in_proximity[0]_raw) channels. Devices named hub-*
(the Unihertz Titan 2 sensor hub bridge) are listed first and become the
default sensors; any other IIO device with these channels works as well.

Values are (raw + offset) * scale with the mount matrix applied, converted
to Android units: m/s^2 (negated: Linux IIO reports an upright device as
y < 0, Android as +g; ATL_IIO_ACCEL_SIGN=1 keeps the IIO sign), rad/s, uT
(gauss * 100), lux; proximity is a distance in cm: hub-prox reports
closeness 0..5 (= 5 - cm, maxRange 5), other devices are near (0) when raw
exceeds in_proximity_nearlevel and far (maxRange) otherwise.

While a sensor has listeners, a daemon thread of its own polls it at the
shortest requested period (SENSOR_DELAY_* or microseconds, 10 ms minimum,
50 ms for the on-change light/proximity sensors) and posts SensorEvents
(with timestamp and accuracy) to each listener's Handler, the main looper
if none was given. Every listener gets events at its own rate, a slow
handler gets the latest sample instead of a growing queue, on-change
sensors report the current value on registration and then only changes,
and the thread ends when the last listener is unregistered.

API: getSensorList (incl. TYPE_ALL), getDefaultSensor (null when there is
no such sensor, like Android; TYPE_ORIENTATION is still emulated from the
location bearing), all registerListener overloads, unregisterListener,
flush (false), the SENSOR_DELAY/SENSOR_STATUS/AXIS/GRAVITY/LIGHT/... constants
and the static helpers getRotationMatrix, getOrientation, getInclination,
getAltitude, remapCoordinateSystem, getRotationMatrixFromVector and
getQuaternionFromVector. Sensor gets the public REPORTING_MODE_* values,
getReportingMode, getMaxDelay, getStringType, isWakeUpSensor, ...;
SensorEvent gets accuracy and timestamp; SensorEventListener gets
onAccuracyChanged (called once before the first event).

The old native accelerometer code (src/api-impl-jni/sensors) is removed;
android_os_Vibrator.c included its header by mistake and now includes its
own.

